<div id="analysis">
  <% common_stat_classes =
    "font-zabal font-black text-4xl mx-auto text-center text-stone-800 dark:text-zinc-100" %>
  <.async_result :let={analysis} assign={@analysis}>
    <:loading>
      <div class="flex justify-center items-center">
        <.spinner size="lg" class="text-brand-500" />
      </div>
    </:loading>
    <:failed :let={_reason}>Failed to load analysis</:failed>

    <h1 class={common_stat_classes <> " text-4xl my-8"}>
      Analysis
    </h1>
    
    <!-- Metric Descriptions -->
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto mb-8 space-y-2" id="metric-descriptions">
      <div class="bg-white dark:bg-zinc-800 rounded-lg shadow p-3 cursor-pointer hover:shadow-lg transition-shadow" data-metric="Consistency">
        <div class="flex items-start gap-2">
          <span class="text-stone-400 dark:text-zinc-500 cursor-help group relative" title="Calculation">
            <span class="invisible group-hover:visible absolute right-6 top-0 w-80 bg-gray-900 text-white text-xs rounded p-3 z-10 whitespace-pre-line leading-relaxed">1. Sort rating history by timestamp
2. Extract all rating values
3. Calculate differences between consecutive ratings
4. Calculate average rating change
5. Calculate standard deviation of changes
6. Invert score: 100 - std_dev (capped at 100)
Result: Lower volatility = higher consistency score</span>
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-5 w-5 mt-0.5" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor">
              <path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M18 10a8 8 0 11-16 0 8 8 0 0116 0zm-7-4a1 1 0 11-2 0 1 1 0 012 0zM9 9a1 1 0 000 2v3a1 1 0 001 1h1a1 1 0 100-2v-3a1 1 0 00-1-1H9z" clip-rule="evenodd" />
            </svg>
          </span>
          <div class="flex-1">
            <div>
              <span class={common_stat_classes <> " text-base font-medium"}>Consistency:</span>
              <span class={common_stat_classes <> " text-lg font-bold ml-2"}><%= Float.round(analysis.consistency, 1) %></span>
            </div>
            <span class="text-stone-600 dark:text-zinc-300"> How stable your performance is across games. Higher scores mean fewer rating swings.</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-white dark:bg-zinc-800 rounded-lg shadow p-3 cursor-pointer hover:shadow-lg transition-shadow" data-metric="Recovery">
        <div class="flex items-start gap-2">
          <span class="text-stone-400 dark:text-zinc-500 cursor-help group relative" title="Calculation">
            <span class="invisible group-hover:visible absolute right-6 top-0 w-80 bg-gray-900 text-white text-xs rounded p-3 z-10 whitespace-pre-line">
              1. Sort rating history by timestamp
2. Track each losing streak (negative streak values)
3. Record streak length when it breaks (becomes positive)
4. Calculate average losing streak length
5. Normalize: 100 - (avg_streak * 10)
Result: Shorter losing streaks = higher recovery score
            </span>
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-5 w-5 mt-0.5" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor">
              <path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M18 10a8 8 0 11-16 0 8 8 0 0116 0zm-7-4a1 1 0 11-2 0 1 1 0 012 0zM9 9a1 1 0 000 2v3a1 1 0 001 1h1a1 1 0 100-2v-3a1 1 0 00-1-1H9z" clip-rule="evenodd" />
            </svg>
          </span>
          <div class="flex-1">
            <div>
              <span class={common_stat_classes <> " text-base font-medium"}>Recovery:</span>
              <span class={common_stat_classes <> " text-lg font-bold ml-2"}><%= Float.round(analysis.recovery, 1) %></span>
            </div>
            <span class="text-stone-600 dark:text-zinc-300"> How quickly you bounce back from losing streaks. Higher scores mean faster recovery.</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-white dark:bg-zinc-800 rounded-lg shadow p-3 cursor-pointer hover:shadow-lg transition-shadow" data-metric="Momentum">
        <div class="flex items-start gap-2">
          <span class="text-stone-400 dark:text-zinc-500 cursor-help group relative" title="Calculation">
            <span class="invisible group-hover:visible absolute right-6 top-0 w-80 bg-gray-900 text-white text-xs rounded p-3 z-10 whitespace-pre-line">
              1. Sort rating history by timestamp
2. Extract all streak values
3. Filter to positive streaks only (wins)
4. Calculate average winning streak length
5. Normalize: avg_streak * 20 (capped at 100)
Result: Longer winning streaks = higher momentum score
            </span>
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-5 w-5 mt-0.5" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor">
              <path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M18 10a8 8 0 11-16 0 8 8 0 0116 0zm-7-4a1 1 0 11-2 0 1 1 0 012 0zM9 9a1 1 0 000 2v3a1 1 0 001 1h1a1 1 0 100-2v-3a1 1 0 00-1-1H9z" clip-rule="evenodd" />
            </svg>
          </span>
          <div class="flex-1">
            <div>
              <span class={common_stat_classes <> " text-base font-medium"}>Momentum:</span>
              <span class={common_stat_classes <> " text-lg font-bold ml-2"}><%= Float.round(analysis.momentum, 1) %></span>
            </div>
            <span class="text-stone-600 dark:text-zinc-300"> Your ability to maintain winning streaks. Higher scores indicate longer win streaks.</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-white dark:bg-zinc-800 rounded-lg shadow p-3 cursor-pointer hover:shadow-lg transition-shadow" data-metric="Anti-Tilt">
        <div class="flex items-start gap-2">
          <span class="text-stone-400 dark:text-zinc-500 cursor-help group relative" title="Calculation">
            <span class="invisible group-hover:visible absolute right-6 top-0 w-80 bg-gray-900 text-white text-xs rounded p-3 z-10 whitespace-pre-line">
              1. Sort rating history by timestamp
2. Look at consecutive game pairs
3. Count: wins after wins, losses after wins, etc.
4. Calculate win_after_win rate
5. Calculate loss_after_loss rate
6. Score = (win_after_win + (1 - loss_after_loss)) / 2
Result: High wins after wins + low losses after losses = high score
            </span>
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-5 w-5 mt-0.5" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor">
              <path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M18 10a8 8 0 11-16 0 8 8 0 0116 0zm-7-4a1 1 0 11-2 0 1 1 0 012 0zM9 9a1 1 0 000 2v3a1 1 0 001 1h1a1 1 0 100-2v-3a1 1 0 00-1-1H9z" clip-rule="evenodd" />
            </svg>
          </span>
          <div class="flex-1">
            <div>
              <span class={common_stat_classes <> " text-base font-medium"}>Anti-Tilt:</span>
              <span class={common_stat_classes <> " text-lg font-bold ml-2"}><%= Float.round(analysis.anti_tilt, 1) %></span>
            </div>
            <span class="text-stone-600 dark:text-zinc-300"> Mental resilience after losses. Higher scores show you tilt less often.</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-white dark:bg-zinc-800 rounded-lg shadow p-3 cursor-pointer hover:shadow-lg transition-shadow" data-metric="Pressure">
        <div class="flex items-start gap-2">
          <span class="text-stone-400 dark:text-zinc-500 cursor-help group relative" title="Calculation">
            <span class="invisible group-hover:visible absolute right-6 top-0 w-80 bg-gray-900 text-white text-xs rounded p-3 z-10 whitespace-pre-line">
              1. Get rank thresholds (700, 800, 900, 1000, etc.)
2. Sort rating history by timestamp
3. For each game, check if within ±25 of any threshold
4. Count wins and total games in pressure situations
5. Calculate win rate: pressure_wins / pressure_total
6. Convert to 0-100 scale
Result: Higher win rate near thresholds = higher clutch score
            </span>
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-5 w-5 mt-0.5" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor">
              <path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M18 10a8 8 0 11-16 0 8 8 0 0116 0zm-7-4a1 1 0 11-2 0 1 1 0 012 0zM9 9a1 1 0 000 2v3a1 1 0 001 1h1a1 1 0 100-2v-3a1 1 0 00-1-1H9z" clip-rule="evenodd" />
            </svg>
          </span>
          <div class="flex-1">
            <div>
              <span class={common_stat_classes <> " text-base font-medium"}>Pressure:</span>
              <span class={common_stat_classes <> " text-lg font-bold ml-2"}><%= Float.round(analysis.pressure_performance, 1) %></span>
            </div>
            <span class="text-stone-600 dark:text-zinc-300"> Win rate when near rank thresholds (±25 rating). Higher scores mean you perform better when your rank is on the line.</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-white dark:bg-zinc-800 rounded-lg shadow p-3 cursor-pointer hover:shadow-lg transition-shadow" data-metric="Efficiency">
        <div class="flex items-start gap-2">
          <span class="text-stone-400 dark:text-zinc-500 cursor-help group relative" title="Calculation">
            <span class="invisible group-hover:visible absolute right-6 top-0 w-80 bg-gray-900 text-white text-xs rounded p-3 z-10 whitespace-pre-line">
              1. Sort rating history by timestamp
2. Get first rating and last rating
3. Calculate rating change: last - first
4. Calculate rating per game: change / games_played
5. Normalize: (rating_per_game + 5) * 10
6. Cap between 0 and 100
Result: More rating gained per game = higher efficiency score
            </span>
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-5 w-5 mt-0.5" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor">
              <path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M18 10a8 8 0 11-16 0 8 8 0 0116 0zm-7-4a1 1 0 11-2 0 1 1 0 012 0zM9 9a1 1 0 000 2v3a1 1 0 001 1h1a1 1 0 100-2v-3a1 1 0 00-1-1H9z" clip-rule="evenodd" />
            </svg>
          </span>
          <div class="flex-1">
            <div>
              <span class={common_stat_classes <> " text-base font-medium"}>Efficiency:</span>
              <span class={common_stat_classes <> " text-lg font-bold ml-2"}><%= Float.round(analysis.rating_efficiency, 1) %></span>
            </div>
            <span class="text-stone-600 dark:text-zinc-300"> How much rating you gain per game played. Higher scores mean faster climbing.</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-white dark:bg-zinc-800 rounded-lg shadow p-3 cursor-pointer hover:shadow-lg transition-shadow" data-metric="Versatility">
        <div class="flex items-start gap-2">
          <span class="text-stone-400 dark:text-zinc-500 cursor-help group relative" title="Calculation">
            <span class="invisible group-hover:visible absolute right-6 top-0 w-80 bg-gray-900 text-white text-xs rounded p-3 z-10 whitespace-pre-line">
              1. Calculate total games across all civs
2. Set min games threshold: max(5, total * 0.05)
3. Filter to civs with games >= threshold
4. Count civs with >50% win rate
5. Calculate: (good_civs / civs_played_enough) * 100
Result: Higher % of well-played civs = higher versatility score
            </span>
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-5 w-5 mt-0.5" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor">
              <path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M18 10a8 8 0 11-16 0 8 8 0 0116 0zm-7-4a1 1 0 11-2 0 1 1 0 012 0zM9 9a1 1 0 000 2v3a1 1 0 001 1h1a1 1 0 100-2v-3a1 1 0 00-1-1H9z" clip-rule="evenodd" />
            </svg>
          </span>
          <div class="flex-1">
            <div>
              <span class={common_stat_classes <> " text-base font-medium"}>Versatility:</span>
              <span class={common_stat_classes <> " text-lg font-bold ml-2"}><%= Float.round(analysis.versatility, 1) %></span>
            </div>
            <span class="text-stone-600 dark:text-zinc-300"> Success across multiple civilizations. Higher scores mean you excel with more civs.</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <canvas id="analysis-chart" phx-hook="Analysis" data-points={}></canvas>
  </.async_result>
</div>
